<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Copel begun.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Copel begun.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Caspian Securities said it started coverage of Parana state power utility Copel with a market-performer rating.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Although we believe Copel is one of the most attractive regional utilities based on its efficiency, strategic position and demand growth, we do not expect its stock appreciation to exceed our 1997 forecast for the Brazilian market at 30 percent,&quot; Caspian said in a report.</p>
<p>-- It also said it estimates the firm's 1996 net income at 174.5 million reais, or 0.72 reais per 1,000 shares, up 69 percent over 1995 results, excluding extraordinary items.</p>
<p>-- Copel common shares traded at 11.15 reais shortly before market's close on Friday.</p>
<p>((-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
